// **the template and the instantiation are in different files**, which is the case a template sharing a
// file with its instance cannot cover. `array<T>::get` is declared in the stdlib and instantiated here, so
// the location it aborts with has to name the stdlib file - the file it was *written* in - and not this one
//
// it is baked into the message as a constant, and the definition is `t_odr_shared`, so getting this from the
// ambient file being emitted would make two units' copies of one symbol disagree
array<int32> $numbers = [1, 2, 3];

echo $numbers->get(0);
echo $numbers->get(7);
